-- title:
--   Divisor-generator criterion for the base-changed modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $M$ be a non-zero natural number, and let $T$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$. Write $\mathrm{jq}$ for the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}(q) \in \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$, where $\mathrm{jNumQ}$ is the power series $\mathrm{jNum}$ with its integer coefficients mapped into $\mathbb{Q}$; write $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d$ for the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ that multiplies all exponents by $d$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$; and write $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$ for the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!) \to L(\!(q)\!)$ applying $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ to each coefficient. Assume that for every non-zero natural number $d$ dividing $M$ the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L\,(\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,\mathrm{jq})$ lies in $T$. The conclusion is the containment $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M) \le T$ of intermediate fields, where $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M$ is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set $\{\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,\mathrm{jq} : d \mid M,\ d \neq 0\}$, and $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L$ of an intermediate field $F_0 \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ is the intermediate field of $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$.
--
--   This is the generation criterion for the base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion model of the full modular function field of level $M$: to contain $L\cdot F_M$ it suffices to contain the expansions $j(q^{d})$ for the divisors $d$ of $M$. It is used when exhibiting concrete presentations of these fields, for instance in the construction of a finite-dimensional or number-field presentation of the level structure and in the reduction of cusp charts in characteristic $p$.
